spec:
  grid: 10-18 rows x 10-17 cols
  divider:
    color: 5 [observed]
    shape: L from top-left; fills row 3 cols 0..C and col C rows 0..3
    row: always 3 [observed]; legend height = 3 rows
    col: 7-11, scales with number of templates
  legend:
    region: rows 0..2, cols 0..C-1 (inside the L)
    templates: 2-4 distinct 4-connected polyominoes, each a unique non-bg/non-divider/non-query color
    template_size: 2-5 cells, bbox fits in 3 rows
    shapes: all canonically distinct under 8-fold rotation/reflection
    spacing: 1-col gap between template bboxes [observed]
  query:
    color: 3 [observed]; exactly one query color
    count: 3-12 sprites, scattered outside the legend
    placement: mostly below divider row; 0-1 sprites in top-right region (right of divider col, above divider row)
    shapes: each matches exactly one legend template under rotation/reflection; queries appear in varied orientations
    matches_per_template: each template matched by >=1 query
    min_bbox_gap: >=2 cells between any two query sprite bboxes (Chebyshev)
  output:
    same grid; every query-color cell recolored to its matched template's color
    legend, divider, and background unchanged; no color-3 remains

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size (10-18 x 10-17) and num_templates (2-4).
    2. Generate num_templates distinct canonical polyomino shapes (2-5 cells, bbox height <=3).
       Assign each a unique color (not 0, 3, or 5).
    3. Place templates in legend row 0..2, left-to-right with 1-col gaps. Set divider col C = legend_width.
    4. Draw L-shaped divider (color 5): fill row 3 cols 0..C, fill col C rows 0..3.
    5. Pick query count (3-12). For each query, pick a template, choose a random rotation/reflection
       of its shape, and place in the query area (below row 3, plus optionally 0-1 in top-right).
       Ensure >=2 Chebyshev gap between all query bboxes and no overlap with divider/legend.
       Ensure every template is matched by >=1 query.
    6. Color all placed query sprites with the matched template color (this is the output).
    7. To produce input, recolor all query sprites to color 3.
